{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.FiberAdjointInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.FiberAdjointInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.fiber_adjoint_involution_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.fiber_adjoint_involution_exists","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L97-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolutionContext.exists_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolutionContext.exists_inv","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolutionContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolutionContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolutionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolutionContext","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L69-L93","doc":"**Existence of the fibre–adjoint involution.**  The structure\n`FiberAdjointInvolution` already bundles the genuine content (the orbit\nembedding `σ`, its antipode-induced involution with `τ_Ad ≫ τ_Ad = id`,\nthe embedding/involution compatibility, and the monomorphism property).\nThe claim asserts that this bundle is *inhabited* for every\nFrobenius–Hopf datum — not the degenerate `∃ inv, True`.\n\nConstructing the witness (the coadjoint-orbit embedding `P(V) ↪ Ad(A)`\nand the antipode-induced `τ_Ad` in a general monoidal category) needs\nmassive infrastructure (categorical machinery beyond the current `QOU.Basic` API)\nthat cannot be added as a simple class field, so the body is left as an honest `sorry`.\n\nThe conclusion pins `adjointObj = fh.obj`: the adjoint bundle `Ad(A)` is\ncarried by the algebra object `A` itself. Without that constraint every\nfield can be taken to be the identity on `𝟙_ C`, which satisfies\n`involution_sq`, `orbit_involution_compat` and `orbit_mono` trivially and\nnever mentions `fh` — so bare `Nonempty (FiberAdjointInvolution C fh)` is\nprovable for *every* category and datum, and asserts nothing. (That\ndegenerate witness was what this declaration shipped until 2026-08-09;\nit is the same emptiness as `∃ inv, True`, reached by a different route.\nSee `docs/audits/2026-08-09-inhabitation-is-a-weak-discriminator.md`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.orbit_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.orbit_mono","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L66-L66","doc":"**(Part 3)** The embedding is a monomorphism: the orbit map\nis injective, so `P(V)` is faithfully represented inside `Ad(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.orbit_involution_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.orbit_involution_compat","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L63-L63","doc":"**(Part 2)** The embedding is compatible with the involution:\nrestricting `τ_Ad` to the image of `σ` recovers `σ`.\nThis means `σ` determines each from the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.involution_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.involution_sq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L59-L59","doc":"`τ_Ad` is an involution: `τ_Ad ≫ τ_Ad = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.involution","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The involution morphism `τ_Ad : Ad(A) ⟶ Ad(A)`, induced by the\nantipode `S : A ⟶ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.orbit_embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.orbit_embed","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L54-L54","doc":"**(Part 1)** The orbit embedding `σ : P(V) ↪ Ad(A)`, realising\n`P(V)` as a coadjoint orbit of a highest-weight vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.projLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.projLine","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The projective line object `P(V)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The adjoint bundle object `Ad(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FiberAdjointInvolution","kind":"structure","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.lean#L28-L67","doc":"**Fibre–adjoint-fibre involution** `σ : P(V) ↪ Ad(A)`.\n\nThe Frobenius self-duality `A ≅ A∨` identifies the projective line\nobject `P(V)` with a coadjoint orbit inside `Ad(A)`.  Three parts:\n\n1. `P(V)` embeds in `Ad(A)` as the coadjoint orbit of a highest-weight\n   vector.\n2. The embedding `σ` is an involution: it determines `P(V)` from\n   `Ad(A)` and vice versa.\n3. Non-degeneracy of the Frobenius pairing forces the observability\n   condition `Hom(𝟙, Ad(A)) = 0`.\n\nIn the archimedean realisation: `σ` is the identification\n`CP¹ ≅ S² ⊂ su(2)` (unit sphere under Killing form).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:fiber-adjoint-involution}`\nRef: [lusztig1993] ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fiber-adjoint-involution","label":"prop:fiber-adjoint-involution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fiber-adjoint-involution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}